- Major themes emerging: political denunciation and injustice, social jealousy and conspiracy, love interrupted by state power, class and local loyalties, the cruelty/arbitrariness of authority.
- Tone: mixes local Marseilles color/folksy detail (Catalans, La Canebière) with rising political suspense; Dumas uses social scenes (wedding, tavern) to set up betrayal.

